#! ia 1.0

@capability run-method
  meaning
    says "Work with run records under the IA methodology: the run-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a run. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a run?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook run-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook run-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with run records, each a governed run identity, status, owner and declared phase, which declaring does not start: orient through ia position --word run and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with run records?"
  subject
    subject-word run
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word run at the seat the work concerns, read the run records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary run --schema for the sections and fields a run carries."
      Inference means "Read the run's identity, owner, status and declared phase, and the runs before it on the same work."
      Decision means "run is a word of session-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/session-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these run records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the run must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide which run the work belongs to and which phase it is in."
      Decision means "Extend an existing run through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the run will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the run; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the run's identity, owner and status; declaring a run starts nothing."
      Decision means "Change run records only through ia preview run <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Update the run's status from the evidence, and attribute a failure to its cause: the instructions, the work or the environment."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the run, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
